{"type":"Film","id":"FR2014_034","slug":"fr2014-034-diplomatie","title":{"native":"Diplomatie","english":"Diplomacy"},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2014-03-05","year":2014},"filmType":"Fiction film","directors":[{"id":"Volker Schlöndorff","slug":"volker-schlondorff","name":"Volker Schlöndorff","birthYear":1939,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[]}],"genre":["Historical film (Heritage Film)"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://medias.unifrance.org/medias/29/207/118557/format_page/diplomatie.jpg","trailerUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qivQ-Pp1MDo"},"synopsis":{"native":"La nuit du 24 au 25 août 1944. Le sort de Paris est entre les mains du Général von Choltitz, Gouverneur du Grand Paris, qui se prépare, sur ordre d’Hitler, à faire sauter la capitale. Issu d’une longue lignée de militaires prussiens, le général n’a jamais eu d’hésitation quand il fallait obéir aux ordres. C’est tout cela qui préoccupe le consul suédois Nordling lorsqu’il gravit l’escalier secret qui le conduit à la suite du Général à l’hôtel Meurice. Les ponts sur la Seine et les principaux monuments de Paris, Le Louvre, Notre-Dame, la Tour Eiffel ... - sont minés et prêts à exploser. Utilisant toutes les armes de la diplomatie, le consul va essayer de convaincre le général de ne pas exécuter l’ordre de destruction.","english":"The night of August 24, 1944. The fate of Paris is in the hands of General von Choltitz, governor of Grand Paris, who is preparing, on Hitler’s orders, to blow up the French capital. The descendent of a long line of Prussian military men, the general has never had any hesitation when it came to obeying orders. This is what’s on Swedish consul Raoul Nordling’s mind as he takes the secret staircase that leads to General von Choltitz’s suite at the Hôtel Meurice. The bridges on the Seine and the major monuments of Paris (including the Louvre, Notre Dame, the Eiffel Tower) are mined with explosives, ready to be detonated. Armed with all the weapons of diplomacy, the consul will try to convince the general not to follow Hitler’s order of destruction."},"production":[{"country":"France","share":"Majority coproducer"},{"country":"Germany","share":"Minority coproducer"}],"characters":[{"id":"FR2014_034_01","film":"FR2014_034","person":{"id":"Niels Arestrup","slug":"niels-arestrup","name":"Niels Arestrup","birthYear":1949,"deathYear":2024,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[{"film":{"slug":"fr2017-155-au-revoir-la-haut","title":{"native":"Au revoir là-haut"}},"year":2018,"award":"César du cinéma","category":"Best Supporting Actor","result":"Nominated"},{"film":{"slug":"fr2014-034-diplomatie","title":{"native":"Diplomatie"}},"year":2015,"award":"César du cinéma","category":"Best Actor Male","result":"Nominated"}]},"age":"3: Third Age (60-75)","gender":"Male identifying","sexuality":"Heterosexual","origin":"White Western European","class":"Upper class","profession":"Employed","ability":"Able-bodied","assistedMobility":"No"},{"id":"FR2014_034_02","film":"FR2014_034","person":{"id":"André Dussollier","slug":"andre-dussollier","name":"André Dussollier","birthYear":1946,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]},"age":"3: Third Age (60-75)","gender":"Male identifying","sexuality":"Heterosexual","origin":"White Western European","class":"Upper class","profession":"Employed","ability":"Able-bodied","assistedMobility":"No"}],"roles":[{"person":{"id":"André Dussollier","slug":"andre-dussollier","name":"André Dussollier","birthYear":1946,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]},"role":"Leading actor"},{"person":{"id":"Burghart Klaußner","slug":"burghart-klaussner","name":"Burghart Klaußner","birthYear":1949,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Germany","awards":[{"film":{"slug":"de2015-094-der-staat-gegen-fritz-bauer","title":{"native":"Der Staat gegen Fritz Bauer"}},"year":2016,"award